WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.417 --> 00:00:01.793
- Are you rolling, Jimmy?

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.837
- What does my hair look like?
- Yep.

00:00:03.879 --> 00:00:05.714
Where is makeup and hair, by the way?

00:00:05.756 --> 00:00:07.424
[laughter]

00:00:07.466 --> 00:00:11.720
[upbeat music]

00:00:11.762 --> 00:00:13.639
"Long Way Up" is the third part

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.224
of our motorcycle adventures,

00:00:15.265 --> 00:00:17.100
Charley Boorman and I.

00:00:17.142 --> 00:00:18.936
- We've done "Round,"
and we've done "Down,"

00:00:18.977 --> 00:00:20.812
and now we were looking to do "Up."

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:23.440
- We decided to go from the very bottom
of South America

00:00:23.482 --> 00:00:24.816
up to Los Angeles.

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.944
It's a really long way up, this one.

00:00:26.985 --> 00:00:28.654
Charley and I met on a movie.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:31.073
We both had very small babies,

00:00:31.114 --> 00:00:32.950
and we're both madly into motorbikes.

00:00:32.991 --> 00:00:35.494
And so the sort of combination
of those two things

00:00:35.536 --> 00:00:37.162
made us very fast friends.

00:00:37.204 --> 00:00:38.622
- [laughs]
- All right.

00:00:38.664 --> 00:00:39.831
She's alive.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.625
We complement each other really well.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:44.670
If I'm down,
he tends to sort of pull me up

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.964
and vice versa.

00:00:47.005 --> 00:00:48.924
- And Ewan moved over to the states,

00:00:48.966 --> 00:00:52.094
and our paths separated for a while.

00:00:52.135 --> 00:00:56.139
About 2016, got clipped by a car,
smashed my legs up to pieces,

00:00:56.181 --> 00:00:59.059
and it took me a couple of years
to walk again properly.

00:00:59.101 --> 00:01:02.104
I wanted to get myself better enough
to get back on the motorbike.

00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:04.940
- Our adventures,
it's what makes him feel alive.

00:01:04.982 --> 00:01:07.109
- The chemistry that those two guys
have is--

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:08.735
you know, you can't create that stuff,

00:01:08.777 --> 00:01:10.070
so we just capture it.

00:01:10.112 --> 00:01:13.448
- We'd always spoken about wanting to do
another "Long Way."

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:15.826
- Charley's motorcycle accident

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:17.077
really was the catalyst

00:01:17.119 --> 00:01:18.829
for getting us all back together again.

00:01:19.955 --> 00:01:22.082
- Good luck, my good friend.
- You too, Charley, good luck.

00:01:22.124 --> 00:01:24.793
I couldn't be happier than to be doing
another one with you.

00:01:24.835 --> 00:01:26.211
It's great.
- Aw.

00:01:26.253 --> 00:01:28.422
You know, we're sitting there,
"Well, what bike do we go on?"

00:01:28.463 --> 00:01:31.258
And we sort of came up with this idea
of going electric.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.510
- This is the first one.
- The first one, man.

00:01:33.552 --> 00:01:34.803
- Think we just plug in?

00:01:34.845 --> 00:01:37.055
Oh, it's going up.
Look, it's working, it's working.

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:41.935
Charley and I, we wanted to do this trip
on electric bikes because it's the future.

00:01:41.977 --> 00:01:44.104
It's opened my mind up
to what is going on in the world.

00:01:44.146 --> 00:01:46.398
Hello.
- Hello, mate.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:50.903
- Harley is pushing into this new realm
of electric-powered motorcycles.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:53.113
We rode prototype models.

00:01:53.155 --> 00:01:56.408
You could see they completely
started again with the suspension.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.493
How long will it take me
to break an indicator?

00:01:58.535 --> 00:02:00.162
- It stalled?
- Ooh.

00:02:01.246 --> 00:02:02.331
- An hour.

00:02:02.372 --> 00:02:04.291
[laughter]

00:02:04.333 --> 00:02:06.210
- Rolling!
- Three, two, one.

00:02:06.251 --> 00:02:08.295
[music continues]

00:02:08.337 --> 00:02:11.423
- Traveling electric, you have to
approach it in a slightly different way.

00:02:11.465 --> 00:02:15.302
- The challenge is trying to get
the miles done

00:02:15.344 --> 00:02:18.555
on a bike that really had a range
of just over 100 miles.

00:02:18.597 --> 00:02:20.474
- We've run out of battery.

00:02:20.516 --> 00:02:21.892
With 10 miles to go.

00:02:21.934 --> 00:02:23.227
- The conditions had to be right.

00:02:23.268 --> 00:02:24.561
Oh, man, it's ice.

00:02:24.603 --> 00:02:27.189
As soon as it got colder,
we've got less miles.

00:02:27.231 --> 00:02:30.776
- We hadn't really realized how much
the batteries are affected

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:32.528
by the cold.

00:02:32.569 --> 00:02:34.029
[music stops]

00:02:34.071 --> 00:02:35.697
Shut down again.

00:02:35.739 --> 00:02:38.116
- Think it's the cold,
that's why it won't charge.

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:42.120
In some of these remote places,
we needed to have a bike that could

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:44.164
plug into a wall anywhere.

00:02:44.206 --> 00:02:45.374
Boom.

00:02:45.415 --> 00:02:48.544
I'm not sure whether
they're very good charges,

00:02:48.585 --> 00:02:50.379
and I feel like probably they're not.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.339
But if we didn't have
two separate circuits,

00:02:52.381 --> 00:02:54.675
we couldn't really charge both bikes
at the same time.

00:02:54.716 --> 00:02:58.595
Came on this big multi-country adventure
with a travel plight.

00:02:58.637 --> 00:03:00.973
And that was tricky.
- 100%.

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:02.891
I'm happy about that.

00:03:02.933 --> 00:03:05.686
And it was a real steep learning curve
to figure it out,

00:03:05.727 --> 00:03:07.521
but once you put your helmet on
and you get going,

00:03:07.563 --> 00:03:09.857
everything else washes away.

00:03:09.898 --> 00:03:11.233
It's beautiful.

00:03:11.275 --> 00:03:13.360
You start thinking about where you are.

00:03:13.402 --> 00:03:14.987
- On the way to Machu Picchu.

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:16.697
Ooh.
[laughs]

00:03:16.738 --> 00:03:19.241
I've always wanted to see it.
[whispers] Wow.

00:03:19.283 --> 00:03:21.159
And I can't really believe we're here.

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:22.828
[indistinct chatter]

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:24.538
[music continues]

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:26.999
When you get out in the world,

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.001
you just find the kindness of people.

00:03:30.669 --> 00:03:33.505
It makes you feel very nice
about humanity.

00:03:34.506 --> 00:03:36.300
They gave us lunch,

00:03:36.341 --> 00:03:39.094
and now we're siphoning their electricity
and eating their food.

00:03:40.804 --> 00:03:42.764
Just so beautiful riding along
with Charley.

00:03:42.806 --> 00:03:45.517
It's been amazing.
Amazing.

00:03:45.559 --> 00:03:47.769
The nicest thing about it,
really, is to get

00:03:47.811 --> 00:03:49.563
to spend that time
with your best friend.

00:03:49.605 --> 00:03:51.064
You look good in that one, Charley.

00:03:51.106 --> 00:03:53.233
- It changed both of our lives forever.

00:03:54.526 --> 00:03:59.364
- We've crossed so much of the Earth
on our motorbikes together.

00:04:00.574 --> 00:04:01.950
It made us very close.

00:04:04.786 --> 00:04:06.872
[music concludes]

